<Base title="Privacy Policy | Oculivo" description="Learn how Oculivo and RomyLabs handle website, account, practice, communication, analytics, and support information.">
<main>
<section class="hero-dark page-hero"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Oculivo is a RomyLabs product. This page explains the categories of information used by the public website and the Oculivo service. Customer data inside Oculivo is also governed by the applicable subscription, service, business associate, or other written agreement when one applies.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-light depth-section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="depth-top"><span class="eyebrow">How information is handled</span><div class="depth-title"><h2>Built around the practice<br/>and its instructions.</h2><p>Oculivo processes practice data to provide the workflows the customer enables. We do not use this page to promise a compliance certification or legal status that has not been established in a signed agreement.</p></div></div>
  <div class="depth-cards">
    <article class="depth-card"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Information we receive</h3><p>Account and staff details, practice and patient information entered by authorized users, documents, communications, scheduling and operational records, support requests, and basic website analytics may be processed when the corresponding feature is used.</p><small>Only the information needed for enabled workflows</small></article>
    <article class="depth-card"><span class="num">02</span><h3>How it is used</h3><p>Information is used to provide the Oculivo service, authenticate users, operate requested workflows, support customers, secure the platform, troubleshoot problems, improve reliability, and measure public website performance.</p><small>Service delivery, security, support and measurement</small></article>
    <article class="depth-card"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Providers and integrations</h3><p>Oculivo may use contracted infrastructure and communication providers for hosting, authentication, storage, analytics, email, SMS, voice, fax, AI, and other features selected by the customer. Those providers process information only as needed for the enabled service.</p><small>Integration use depends on customer configuration</small></article>
  </div>
  <div class="policy-copy">
    <h2>Practice data and access</h2><p>Oculivo uses organization-scoped access controls, database row-level security, private storage for protected files, and role-aware permissions. Customers are responsible for granting access only to appropriate workforce members and for maintaining accurate account information.</p>
    <h2>Website analytics</h2><p>The public Oculivo website uses Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity to understand site usage and improve performance. These services may receive device, browser, page-view, interaction, and similar analytics information according to their own terms and privacy practices.</p>
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Retention depends on the type of information, the customer's configuration, legal and contractual requirements, and the applicable service agreement. Authorized customers may contact RomyLabs about account, access, retention, export, or deletion requests.</p>
    <h2>Security</h2><p>No internet service can guarantee absolute security. Oculivo uses technical and organizational safeguards designed to reduce unauthorized access, including authenticated access, tenant-scoped database policies, private storage, and audit-oriented controls.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy or data-handling questions, email <a href="mailto:info@romylabs.com">info@romylabs.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</Base>
